00:29:14.680 --> 00:29:15.680
floating robot body.

00:29:15.940 --> 00:29:17.580
I prefer George Lopez

00:29:17.580 --> 00:29:19.380
from Sharkboy and Lavagirl.

00:29:19.600 --> 00:29:21.400
Is that what happens?

00:29:21.400 --> 00:29:23.040
Wow, I really got to watch that movie.

00:29:23.100 --> 00:29:25.400
You know what's funny? I never saw Sharkboy and Lavagirl,

00:29:25.480 --> 00:29:26.640
but I always thought that

00:29:26.640 --> 00:29:27.680
that George Lopez thing

00:29:27.680 --> 00:29:28.560
was from Spy Kids.

00:29:28.740 --> 00:29:29.980
And then very recently,

00:29:29.980 --> 00:29:31.920
I saw the clip from Sharkboy and Lavagirl,

00:29:31.960 --> 00:29:34.460
and I'm like, oh, I don't even know why this is in my brain.

00:29:34.460 --> 00:29:35.520
I never saw this movie.

00:29:35.700 --> 00:29:40.160
I thought that Sharkboy and Lavagirl

00:29:40.160 --> 00:29:42.940
was just me misremembering Spy Kids.

00:29:43.320 --> 00:29:44.860
And I thought that for sure

00:29:44.860 --> 00:29:47.980
that was just, like, a spinoff of the Spy Kids.

00:29:48.200 --> 00:29:49.100
I think it is, right?

00:29:49.520 --> 00:29:51.320
I don't know. Is it? It's not?

00:29:51.320 --> 00:29:54.640
It's its own thing? I don't think that the Spy Kids

00:29:54.640 --> 00:29:56.460
ever interact with them.

00:29:56.700 --> 00:29:58.420
Like, I'm not saying that the same studios

00:29:58.420 --> 00:29:59.720
don't own them. Oh,

00:29:59.840 --> 00:30:00.920
it's the same director. Yeah,

00:30:00.920 --> 00:30:02.420
it's Robert Rodriguez. Right,

00:30:02.660 --> 00:30:03.560
yeah, same director.

00:30:03.860 --> 00:30:05.260
But, Spy Kids,

00:30:05.380 --> 00:30:08.020
you know, has way more going on in it.

00:30:08.240 --> 00:30:09.900
There's a lot of philosophical stuff

00:30:09.900 --> 00:30:10.860
going on in Spy Kids.

00:30:11.100 --> 00:30:14.160
Is there? There actually is.

00:30:14.380 --> 00:30:15.500
I can't remember,

00:30:15.760 --> 00:30:16.900
nobody wants to see me

00:30:16.900 --> 00:30:19.580
Google the quote, but there is a really heavy quote

00:30:19.580 --> 00:30:21.520
from the villain in the first Spy Kids

00:30:21.520 --> 00:30:23.840
that is like, they said that in a kids movie?

00:30:24.100 --> 00:30:25.160
What was it like,

00:30:25.160 --> 00:30:27.300
you don't do the spy

00:30:27.300 --> 00:30:28.900
if you can't do the...

00:30:28.900 --> 00:30:31.000
They were like, seize the means of production.

00:30:31.440 --> 00:30:32.620
Oh. No,

00:30:32.740 --> 00:30:33.660
definitely not that.

00:30:33.800 --> 00:30:35.460
No, it was like way more deep than that.

00:30:35.920 --> 00:30:37.460
I'll find it by the end of the episode.

00:30:37.740 --> 00:30:39.240
Right now, I just want to talk more about the game

00:30:39.240 --> 00:30:40.200
because I think that's important.

00:30:41.260 --> 00:30:42.800
Was there any point

00:30:42.800 --> 00:30:45.440
to the whole Mega Man

00:30:45.440 --> 00:30:46.620
choose your own adventure?

00:30:47.160 --> 00:30:48.580
Well, the game was a Mega Man clone.

00:30:48.980 --> 00:30:49.800
Yeah, but like,

00:30:50.440 --> 00:30:52.060
I feel like in Mega Man,

00:30:52.240 --> 00:30:53.860
there's a reason to go

00:30:53.860 --> 00:30:55.080
in a particular order.

00:30:56.180 --> 00:30:57.540
You know, trying to like rock,

00:30:57.640 --> 00:30:58.960
paper, scissors your way through the bosses.

00:30:59.380 --> 00:31:01.260
But in this game, there's,

00:31:01.440 --> 00:31:03.100
you just have the one thing

00:31:04.040 --> 00:31:06.000
and you don't like unlock anything

00:31:06.000 --> 00:31:07.240
after anything. So.

00:31:07.780 --> 00:31:09.520
Yeah, it's not like if you suck at the level

00:31:09.520 --> 00:31:10.400
that you'll get better

00:31:10.400 --> 00:31:11.920
after doing the other levels.

00:31:11.920 --> 00:31:13.120
Like, you know,

00:31:13.200 --> 00:31:14.840
you still have to like, you still have to complete

00:31:14.840 --> 00:31:15.880
that level eventually.

00:31:16.160 --> 00:31:18.220
Right. I guess the only point to it

00:31:18.220 --> 00:31:19.200
for me then would be what,

00:31:19.320 --> 00:31:21.580
you know, what the effect that is inherent

00:31:21.580 --> 00:31:22.700
to this kind of gameplay,

00:31:22.760 --> 00:31:24.380
which is that if I'm stuck on something,

00:31:24.480 --> 00:31:25.640
I don't, I'm not stuck

00:31:25.640 --> 00:31:26.980
and I can't play any

00:31:26.980 --> 00:31:27.900
of the rest of the game.

00:31:28.240 --> 00:31:29.880
So I guess I, I appreciate that

00:31:29.880 --> 00:31:30.840
in some games

00:31:30.840 --> 00:31:33.120
where I'm like, it's not so linear

00:31:33.120 --> 00:31:34.440
that I can't go try something else.

00:31:34.820 --> 00:31:36.660
That's fine. It's just weird.

00:31:37.040 --> 00:31:38.120
Yeah. It's not really designed

00:31:38.120 --> 00:31:39.180
around it. Yeah.

00:31:40.140 --> 00:31:42.700
You can skip four of the seven bosses

00:31:42.700 --> 00:31:43.580
in this game

00:31:44.220 --> 00:31:45.520
with a glitch.

00:31:45.520 --> 00:31:47.200
It's not like meant by design,

00:31:47.380 --> 00:31:49.140
but on certain stages,

00:31:50.000 --> 00:31:50.960
hitting select

00:31:50.960 --> 00:31:52.560
to detonate your grenades,

00:31:52.800 --> 00:31:54.280
which is one of your power-ups

00:31:54.280 --> 00:31:58.380
that you can collect. Just as the boss door closes behind you,

00:31:58.680 --> 00:31:59.500
kills the boss

00:31:59.500 --> 00:32:00.960
before the fight screen loads

00:32:00.960 --> 00:32:02.300
and it's just over.

00:32:02.560 --> 00:32:04.740
What's interesting is that that only happens

00:32:04.740 --> 00:32:06.660
to four of the seven.

00:32:06.660 --> 00:32:08.720
so like what...

00:32:08.720 --> 00:32:09.860
Are they trying to tell us something?

00:32:10.340 --> 00:32:12.400
Yeah, exactly. Like, does that mean something

00:32:12.400 --> 00:32:13.860
or is it like, did they just,

00:32:14.260 --> 00:32:16.560
does, do the other enemies

00:32:16.560 --> 00:32:17.560
like load differently

00:32:17.560 --> 00:32:19.240
than these and that's what's causing it?

00:32:19.340 --> 00:32:20.400
It's just a weird thing,

00:32:20.520 --> 00:32:21.540
but obviously very useful

00:32:21.540 --> 00:32:22.360
for speed runs.

00:32:22.540 --> 00:32:23.720
No, no, no. I think like it's,

00:32:23.820 --> 00:32:25.320
you know, four plus seven

00:32:25.320 --> 00:32:26.680
is 11.

00:32:28.780 --> 00:32:29.660
11 commandments.

00:32:31.920 --> 00:32:35.660
So 2,191

00:32:36.500 --> 00:32:38.080
is the year the world ends.

00:32:38.480 --> 00:32:40.160
So that's what they're trying

00:32:40.160 --> 00:32:41.960
to tell us. Yeah, I thought that was

00:32:41.960 --> 00:32:43.160
pretty straightforward.

00:32:43.700 --> 00:32:46.640
Yeah. In the Power Blade manual,

00:32:47.520 --> 00:32:48.700
it tells us

00:32:48.700 --> 00:32:51.460
that we have to restore

00:32:51.460 --> 00:32:53.300
the master computer, right?

00:32:53.420 --> 00:32:54.660
That's how we're going to fix all this,

00:32:55.080 --> 00:32:56.460
you know, beat the aliens,

00:32:56.680 --> 00:32:57.720
restore the master computer.

00:32:57.720 --> 00:32:58.600
Right.

00:32:59.240 --> 00:33:01.580
But the in-game intro

00:33:02.200 --> 00:33:03.460
tells us to destroy

00:33:03.460 --> 00:33:04.540
the master computer

00:33:04.540 --> 00:33:06.160
and then the ending

00:33:06.160 --> 00:33:08.040
has humanity vowing

00:33:08.040 --> 00:33:09.600
never to hand that much power

00:33:09.600 --> 00:33:10.740
to a machine again.

00:33:12.740 --> 00:33:14.140
So which is it?

00:33:14.340 --> 00:33:15.700
What were we supposed to do?

00:33:15.760 --> 00:33:16.960
Did we learn along the way?

00:33:17.320 --> 00:33:18.760
Well, I didn't finish the game,

00:33:18.900 --> 00:33:21.080
but my, you know,

00:33:21.340 --> 00:33:22.400
again, my interpretation,

00:33:22.760 --> 00:33:24.080
and I think I'm on a roll here,

00:33:25.560 --> 00:33:26.940
is that, you know,

00:33:26.940 --> 00:33:28.620
you kind of have to

00:33:28.620 --> 00:33:29.640
turn it back on

00:33:29.640 --> 00:33:30.780
just to, like,

00:33:30.900 --> 00:33:32.540
remember how to do the things that it does.

00:33:33.180 --> 00:33:35.440
Like, kind of just watch it

00:33:35.440 --> 00:33:36.500
do its thing for a bit,

00:33:36.500 --> 00:33:37.940
and then you can kind of

00:33:37.940 --> 00:33:39.300
wean yourself off of it.

00:33:40.440 --> 00:33:41.880
That's what I would do

00:33:41.880 --> 00:33:43.020
if I were a society

00:33:43.020 --> 00:33:44.380
that has completely

00:33:44.380 --> 00:33:45.600
infantilized itself.

00:33:47.540 --> 00:33:48.900
So, are we saying

00:33:48.900 --> 00:33:50.240
that it, it,

00:33:50.460 --> 00:33:51.840
they destroyed it

00:33:51.840 --> 00:33:53.760
and they're not handing

00:33:53.760 --> 00:33:55.120
that kind of power to it again

00:33:55.120 --> 00:33:56.640
or to any technology again?

00:33:56.700 --> 00:33:57.600
Like, maybe they destroyed it

00:33:57.600 --> 00:33:58.420
and now they'll start

00:33:58.420 --> 00:34:00.180
building technology but not give it

00:34:00.180 --> 00:34:01.100
that kind of power.

00:34:01.760 --> 00:34:03.060
Yes, I think it's that.

00:34:03.820 --> 00:34:05.140
Full butlerian jihad.

00:34:05.500 --> 00:34:07.100
Like, typewriters are okay,

00:34:07.420 --> 00:34:09.260
but not computers anymore.

00:34:09.420 --> 00:34:10.520
Right. And everything has to be analog.

00:34:11.080 --> 00:34:13.640
Right. There has to be an off switch.

00:34:13.640 --> 00:34:15.120
And wood paneling.

00:34:15.400 --> 00:34:16.440
Oh, that's awesome.

00:34:16.720 --> 00:34:18.680
Shoot. That'd be pretty cool. They went, they went like that?

00:34:19.180 --> 00:34:20.380
Yeah. The place is sick.

00:34:21.580 --> 00:34:23.640
In the Japanese version

00:34:23.640 --> 00:34:25.040
of the game, Power Blazer,

00:34:25.980 --> 00:34:27.740
the power meter thing,

00:34:28.700 --> 00:34:29.780
you have to wait,

00:34:30.020 --> 00:34:31.200
like, you have to wait

00:34:31.200 --> 00:34:32.660
for it to drain before you can take

00:34:32.660 --> 00:34:34.580
another shot and it takes a second

00:34:34.580 --> 00:34:35.660
or two to refill.

00:34:35.880 --> 00:34:37.380
So, you can't spam it

00:34:37.380 --> 00:34:38.220
as much as you can

00:34:38.220 --> 00:34:40.180
in this one. And I suppose

00:34:40.180 --> 00:34:41.540
that's a good idea and concept,

00:34:41.740 --> 00:34:43.660
like, to make sure that you can't spam

00:34:43.660 --> 00:34:44.660
your attack in a game

00:34:44.660 --> 00:34:45.480
that maybe you want

00:34:45.480 --> 00:34:47.760
to have, like, more deliberate shots for.

00:34:48.260 --> 00:34:49.540
Except the enemies

00:34:49.540 --> 00:34:51.040
can spam their attacks

00:34:51.040 --> 00:34:52.140
and they can crowd you

00:34:52.140 --> 00:34:53.560
and you'll take multiple hits.

00:34:53.800 --> 00:34:55.500
So, it was really

00:34:55.500 --> 00:34:56.360
just hurting the player.

00:34:56.500 --> 00:34:58.340
So, I guess I'm glad that they turned that off

00:34:58.340 --> 00:35:00.100
in this completely

00:35:00.100 --> 00:35:01.540
different American game.

00:35:02.120 --> 00:35:03.240
And it still, like,

00:35:03.340 --> 00:35:04.780
uses the power meter,

00:35:04.980 --> 00:35:08.060
at least when you have the regular boomerangs,

00:35:08.060 --> 00:35:10.840
in that if you do spam it,

00:35:11.100 --> 00:35:13.300
your subsequent throws

00:35:13.300 --> 00:35:15.680
have much less range.

00:35:15.900 --> 00:35:18.140
So, it's still encouraging

00:35:18.140 --> 00:35:19.300
you not to spam.

00:35:19.560 --> 00:35:20.640
And Power Blade

